+### Instant Bank Payments 
+
+Disputes for Instant Bank Payments don’t map to the same eight categories as other payment methods. Every dispute for Instant Bank Payments uses the same dispute reason, `debit_not_authorized`, with the underlying ACH return code shown as the network reason code.
+
+| Return code | Reason | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| R10 | Unauthorized | The customer claims they didn’t authorize the debit. |
+| R07 | Authorization revoked | The customer revoked an authorization they previously granted. |
+| R08 | Payment stopped | The customer instructed their bank to stop this specific debit. |
+| R11 | Not per terms | The debit wasn’t in accordance with the terms of the authorization. |
+| R29 | Corporate not authorized | A corporate customer advises the debit wasn’t authorized. |
+| R05 | Unauthorized (corporate SEC code) | An unauthorized debit to a consumer account using a corporate SEC code. |
+| R31 | Permissible return | A permissible return entry, for corporate (CCD and CTX) accounts only. |
+
+For the evidence that helps you respond to each return code, see [Disputed Instant Bank Payments](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/link/instant-bank-payments/disputed-payments.md).
+
